title: Linux Update Tracker: Pending updates
agents: linux
catalog: os/misc
license: GPLv2
distribution: https://github.com/KeksDipp/checkmk-plugins
description:
 Lists every package with a pending update: installed and candidate version,
 repository, classification, advisory severity and age. Needs the agent plugin
 {linux_update_tracker}. Supported package managers: APT, DNF, DNF5, YUM and
 Zypper.

 Each package is checked against age limits (default: {WARN} after 2 days,
 {CRIT} after 7 days). The age counts from when the package first had an
 update on this host (newer versions do not reset it), optionally from when the
 current candidate version showed up or from the publish date of the advisory.
 Age rules can set other limits for certain packages, e.g. security updates.

 No updates are filtered by default. Held and phased packages, classifications,
 package names and repositories can be filtered.

 The service also goes {WARN} if the update search or the index refresh fails,
 or if the last successful search or the package index is older than 2 days
 ({CRIT} after 7 days). It is always {WARN} if the plugin cannot write its state
 file, because the package ages would not be tracked then.

discovery:
 One service is created if the agent plugin output is present.
